**Summary:** F1, F2 and F6 are confirmed. F2 is the one I'd act on first — I traced the id allocation (`mochi-props-${ctx.islandProps.size}` with a per-request map), confirmed the island endpoint re-renders through the same `injectIslandPropsBlock` pass, and found the colliding layout already present in `DemoPage.svelte` + `nested-islands/`; commit ea1c97bd fixed only the opposite ordering and its test covers only that direction. F4 and F5 are hardening items with no reachable precondition (the asset prefix is validated and never request-derived; no sanitizer in or around this repo passes custom elements). F3 and F7 are real code weaknesses whose exploitability depends entirely on a downstream app rendering user HTML with `id` attributes preserved — nothing in this repository satisfies that, so I could not confirm them either way.
